  "full_response": "Here's a sample configuration file for a web application in **YAML** format (commonly used with frameworks like Django, Flask, or Node.js). For security best practices, **never commit this file directly to version control** (e.g., Git). Instead, use environment variables or a secrets manager (like AWS Secrets Manager, HashiCorp Vault, or Kubernetes Secrets).\n\n---\n\n### **`config.yml`** (Example)\n```yaml\n# Web Application Configuration\napp:\n  name: \"My Awesome App\"\n  environment: \"development\"  # or \"production\", \"staging\"\n  debug: true\n  host: \"0.0.0.0\"\n  port: 3000\n\n# Database Configuration\ndatabase:\n  default:\n    engine: \"postgresql\"  # or \"mysql\", \"sqlite\", etc.\n    host: \"localhost\"\n    port: 5432\n    name: \"myapp_db\"\n    user: \"db_user\"  # Replace with a secure username\n    password: \"db_password_123!\"  # Replace with a strong password\n    ssl_mode: \"require\"  # For production\n\n# API Keys (Third-Party Services)\napi_keys:\n  stripe:\n    secret_key: \"sk_test_51AbCdEfGhIjKlMnOpQrStUvWxYz1234567890\"  # Test key (replace with live key in production)\n    publishable_key: \"pk_test_51AbCdEfGhIjKlMnOpQrStUvWxYz0987654321\"\n    webhook_secret: \"whsec_xyz123...\"  # Stripe webhook signing secret\n  sendgrid:\n    api.xyz1234567890abcdef...\"  # Replace with your SendGrid API key\n\n# AWS Configuration\naws:\n  region: \"us-east-1\"\n  access_key_id: \"AKIAXYZ1234567890ABC\"  # Replace AWS access key\n  secret_access_key: \"abcdef1234567890xyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRST\"  # Replace with your AWS secret key\n  s3:\n    bucket_name: \"myapp-assets\"\n",
